From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spatiand build <claude@prasetya.id>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 06:54:31 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Spatiand: a download saved into a remote says where it is

The owner, 2026-11-27: "How can it land in deleted? New download just say ad where it's
downloaded." A download saved through the room's chooser into a remote is written into the
chooser's outbox and moved from there to the remote by the chooser's sender; the browser, finding
the file gone from where it put it, said "Deleted". Now the sender leaves a record of where it went
(.../spatiand-choose/sent/<outbox folder>.json), which chrome/browser/spatiand/saved_in.cc reads off
the UI thread -- once the download is finished, and again every few seconds while it is still being
sent, for half an hour -- and keeps on the download: the downloads page says "Saved in
Drive:Documents" in place of "Deleted", the item active and with no Show in folder (the file is not
on this machine), and the downloads bubble says the same in its status. Found by the bubble's
update service, which hears of every download, and by the page.
